\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This is actually an interesting problem because there are already prompt optimizers, but most focus on 
\f1\b making prompts better
\f0\b0 , not 
\f1\b making them smaller while preserving quality
\f0\b0 . I think there's room for a tool aimed at developers who use AI APIs heavily.\
I'd build it as a 
\f1\b desktop-first local application
\f0\b0  that acts as a proxy between your apps and the LLM.\
