\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Interesting Challenge\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 One difficult problem is avoiding 
\f1\b over-optimization
\f0\b0 .\
For example:\
Original:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Always answer in JSON.\
\
Do not include markdown.\
\
Do not explain.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 An optimizer might incorrectly reduce it to:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Return JSON.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf0 That changes behavior by dropping important constraints. A good optimizer should understand when multiple instructions are complementary rather than redundant.\
One way to address this is to have every optimization produce a 
\f1\b confidence score
\f0\b0 . High-confidence changes (like removing exact duplicates) can be applied automatically, while lower-confidence semantic rewrites require user approval.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

